# mental map — with no room to remember a place, the visit keeps its map, and leaving forgets it
#
# A place is remembered as a mental map: the areas stood in, the ways gone by, what was seen, and the
# routines learned there. The anamnesis holds four maps a point, so a body with none holds none. The
# visit in progress still keeps a map of its own (the walk, backtrack and the map view all work), but
# when it ends the map is forgotten — the routine learned with it too — and the next visit finds the
# place unknown again.
#
# One move to the yard, as routine_movement_only.cli: in the visit the yard is on the map; after it,
# nothing is remembered; coming back, the yard is unknown.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Field" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Yard" --organs anamnesis=0

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal move
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-verb move

# The visit holds its map although no slot does.
expect-state map map visited Test Yard
expect-state mental-maps mental-maps used=0 usable=0

observe none
click button
wait 60
advance 12 180
click button
wait mode WorldView 90

# Left, and forgotten: no map, so no routine either.
expect-state mental-maps mental-maps used=0
expect-no-state mental-maps mental-map location=
expect-no-state routines category=goto

travel neighbour
travel-go
wait mode LocationInteraction 120
advance 12 180
click button
wait mode WorldView 90

travel back
travel-go
wait mode LocationInteraction 120
advance 12 180

# Back again: the field it opens in is stood in once more, the yard is unknown.
expect-state map map visited Test Field
expect-no-state map map visited Test Yard
quit
